Subject: [PATCH] net: bootp: use the DHCP server's boot server when no ProxyDHCP answers

With SERVERIP_FROM_PROXYDHCP the boot server and file name are taken only
from a ProxyDHCP answer (a packet without an address for the client). On a
network where the DHCP server itself names the boot server, serverip stays
empty and nothing can be loaded.

Take the parameters from the DHCP server's own answer when no ProxyDHCP
server has set a boot server. A ProxyDHCP answer still takes precedence.
---
diff --git a/net/bootp.c b/net/bootp.c
index f0dc329..0da2ad0 100644
--- a/net/bootp.c
+++ b/net/bootp.c
@@ -183,6 +183,14 @@ static void store_net_params(struct bootp_hdr *bp)
 {
 #if !defined(CONFIG_SERVERIP_FROM_PROXYDHCP)
 	store_bootp_params(bp);
+#else
+	/*
+	 * No ProxyDHCP server has named a boot server: take the one the DHCP
+	 * server itself gives, as a build without SERVERIP_FROM_PROXYDHCP does.
+	 * A ProxyDHCP answer, also a late one, still takes precedence.
+	 */
+	if (!net_server_ip.s_addr)
+		store_bootp_params(bp);
 #endif
 	net_copy_ip(&net_ip, &bp->bp_yiaddr);
 }
